# In-file tests (plans/reference/MEMBER_VISIBILITY.md): a plain module with a
# top-level `test(...)` is collected by `yo test <dir>` — Rust's `#[cfg(test)]
# mod tests` — and its tests may reach the module's private `_count` field and
# private `_bump` helper, which nothing outside `lib/` may. `main.yo` is a
# PROGRAM with its own `main` and an in-file test: the batch drops the
# module's `main` / `export(main)` and supplies its own. The golden keeps the per-test verdict lines and the summary; the
# timing figures are dropped.
stdout_keep=^(  ✓|  ✗|[0-9]+ passed|[0-9]+ failed|error)
timeout=300
